        "title": "Special experiences over cremation",
        "text": "On the date we visited Pashupatinath, we found hundred of people over there... and we just noticed many policemen around. Our guide told us that a high-ranked police official was under cremation. \n\nWe observed the whole process, which was both shocking and interesting. It was the first time seeing this in a short distance. \n\nThere are a lot of Hindus priest. They asked for the photo taking but I did not as I did not know if they would ask for $ after photo. Are they real priest or just some way to get tourist money. Who knows?\n\nApart from these, as we are not hindu, we just can't see much. But, the entrance fee is Rs 500. It is pretty high when compared with other temples in Kathmandu.",
