        "title": "More than I expected, the most shocking place I visited",
        "text": "It was our first day in Nepal, we hired a gide who took us to the pashupatinath temple. The first sight I remember was a body of a dead person carried by his family. I kept walking by a bridge and saw three bodies in fire. It was amazing to see all that people praying and burning their deads. And there was more, the other side of the river, that runs inside the temple, was habitated by Sadus and many, many monkeys.\nI didn't expect to find so many diferent and socking things in that place. If you are in Nepal, must go there.",
