      {
        "review_id": 28684194,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r28684194-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "It's not for everybody--even if we're all headed that way",
        "text": "We got to visit this temple on our first day--and were welcomed by women in red, gathered around a fire, celebrating. It was absolutely fascinating. Much further in, our guide pointed out the river, rather dried up due to lack of rain. Further down...a cremation was going on. Quite a surprise, but still this being a holy place--we saw all sorts of human endeavors--from the celebration of life, to the release into the next world. I don't think it's for everybody, especially the squemish--but hey, it's Nepal. And at the least, it makes for incredible stories.",
