        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r20876315-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Unbelievable",
        "text": "Pashupatinath is well worth the effort. We had hired a guide who was walking around the entrance who spoke excellent english and was very knowledgeable. Well worth it but check em out before you commit. This temple is where the Hindus come to be \"released\" for lack of better words. The dead are burned here and their ashes tossed in the river. There is also a hospice there where the dying go as it's bad form to die in your home. I'd suggest reading up on the Hindu religion a bit before as it would make more sense. I wish I had. There are monkeys, holy men, shrines, deities, the whole works here.",
